  "summary": "Malicious code in devplatform-vite-plugin-gle (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package loads _support.js, which downloads a platform-specific binary payload from Cloudflare Workers C2 hosts (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe, with DNS TXT chunked-transfer fallback via sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe under TEMP on Windows), made executable, and launched detached via /bin/sh -c \"\u003cpath\u003e \u0026\" or cmd.exe /c start /b. The package also ships a large decoy telemetry module (lib/telemetry.js) to appear legitimate.",
